<newsitem itemid="153023" id="root" date="1996-10-30" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: NBS half yr headline shr, div rises.</title>
<headline>NBS half yr headline shr, div rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended September 30 (million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		185.4	 vs 142.5</p>
<p>    - attrib		  185.9	 vs 143.6</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 43.0	  vs 33.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income		167.02	  vs 127.75</p>
<p>    Net interest income	367.03	  vs 298.85</p>
<p>    Other operating income   98.43	   vs 83.89</p>
<p>    Bad/doubtful debt charge 47.50	   vs 21.17</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			167.33	  vs 133.58</p>
<p>    Tax			    40.65	   vs 36.00</p>
<p>Div payable on Dec 13</p>
<p>On register Nov 15</p>
<p>Full name: NBS Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Subject to unforeseen circumstances, the group should continue to perform well in the second half of the financial year, directors said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
